                                                <div class="person-dialog__content">
                                                    <div class="person-dialog__header margin-trim">
                                                        <h2>Rosalind Ford</h2>

                                                                                                                    <h4>Mother</h4>
                                                                                                            </div>

                                                    <div class="person-dialog__bio">
                                                        <p class="type-body-xl"></p>

                                                        <div class="person-dialog__bio__main__text">
                                                            <p>Rosalind read French and Italian at Edinburgh University and holds an MA in Translation.</p>
<p>Theatre credits include: Dorcas Lane in LARK RISE TO CANDLEFORD (Watermill Theatre, Theatre by the Lake); COVEN (Kiln Theatre); IN CLAY (OFFIE Award Winner: Lead Performance in a Musical, Upstairs at the Gatehouse); THE CABINET MINISTER (Menier Chocolate Factory); THE CURIOUS CASE OF BENJAMIN BUTTON, MOTHER COURAGE AND HER CHILDREN (Southwark Playhouse); MISS LITTLEWOOD, BOUNDLESS AS THE SEA (RSC/Cunard); Adriana in THE COMEDY OF ERRORS (Mercury Theatre); Ophelia in HAMLET (Guildford Shakespeare Company); ONCE (UK Tour); GIN CRAZE! (Royal &amp; Derngate); and THESE TREES ARE MADE OF BLOOD (Arcola Theatre).</p>
<p>Workshop credits include: THE CURIOUS CASE OF BENJAMIN BUTTON (ATG); COVEN (Kiln Theatre); THE LOST SOULS CLUB (Mercury Theatre); UNITED WE STAND (The Cockpit); and JOHN BARLEYCORN MUST DIE (Tombola Theatre).</p>

                                                        </div>
                                                    </div>
                                                </div>
                                            </article>
                                        </template>
                                    
                                    


