                                                <div class="person-dialog__content">
                                                    <div class="person-dialog__header margin-trim">
                                                        <h2>Nitai Levi</h2>

                                                                                                                    <h4>Henryk</h4>
                                                                                                            </div>

                                                    <div class="person-dialog__bio">
                                                        <p class="type-body-xl"></p>

                                                        <div class="person-dialog__bio__main__text">
                                                            <p>Training: Royal Academy of Music.</p>
<p>Theatre Credits include: THE HOLY ROSENBERGS (Menier Chocolate Factory); AS YOU LIKE IT (Theatre Royal Bath, dir. Ralph Fiennes); NATASHA, PIERRE &amp; THE GREAT COMET OF 1812, THE BAND&#8217;S VISIT (Donmar Warehouse); A CHRISTMAS CAROL (Sheffield Crucible); THE OTHER BOLEYN GIRL (Chichester Festival Theatre); SCENES FROM RENT (Leicester Curve); TIL IT STOPS (Cockpit Theatre); and SPRING AWAKENING (Edinburgh Fringe).</p>
<p>Workshop Credits include: MANDELA (The Young Vic); ACCOUNTING FOR BEGINNERS (National Theatre); LOST IN LOVE (Runaway Entertainment); and BORDELLO (CDM Productions).</p>
<p>Film &amp; Television Credits include: WE WERE THE LUCKY ONES (Hulu/Disney+); and MASTERS OF THE AIR (Apple TV+).</p>
<p>Concerts include: ROMEO AND JULIET/WEST SIDE STORY (BBC Concert Orchestra, Barbican Centre); and LETTERS HOME (Royal Academy of Music).</p>
<p>Other Credits include: BUÑUEL IN THE LABYRINTH OF THE TURTLES – ORIGINAL SOUNDTRACK (Abbey Road Studios).</p>
<p>As a singer-songwriter, Nitai releases music under the name NITAI.</p>

                                                        </div>
                                                    </div>
                                                </div>
                                            </article>
                                        </template>
                                    
                                    


